<cell id="cell-0"><cell_type>markdown</cell_type># Cryogenic — Offline GPU Music Visualizer

Renders a polished 1080p60 music video from your stems-analysis JSON and the original mp3, using Colab's GPU.

**Before you start:** Runtime → Change runtime type → **GPU** → choose **L4** (best value on Colab Pro) or **A100** (fastest).

Workflow:
1. Run the **Setup** cell once (~1 minute).
2. Check the **GPU sanity** cell confirms an NVIDIA renderer (not llvmpipe).
3. Run the **Upload** cell and drop in your `viz_data_v2.json` and the matching `.mp3`.
4. Run **Render**. ~4–8 min for a 3-min song at 1080p60 on an L4.
5. Preview / download `cryogenic.mp4` from the last cell.</cell id="cell-0">
<cell id="cell-1"><cell_type>markdown</cell_type>## 1. Setup — install GPU OpenGL + ffmpeg + clone repo</cell id="cell-1">
<cell id="cell-2">%%bash
set -e

# --- Core headless EGL/GL libs ---
apt-get -qq update
apt-get -qq install -y libegl1 libgles2 libglvnd0 libgl1 libglib2.0-0 ffmpeg >/dev/null

# --- NVIDIA EGL userspace libs ---
# Without libEGL_nvidia.so.0 on the loader path, libEGL only finds Mesa's ICD
# and moderngl falls back to llvmpipe (~1 fps). The package is
# libnvidia-gl-<MAJOR> where MAJOR matches the running kernel driver, but
# Ubuntu's apt repo doesn't always carry every major Colab ships, so we try
# the exact match first and then fall back to whatever is available.
DRIVER_VER=$(nvidia-smi --query-gpu=driver_version --format=csv,noheader 2>/dev/null | head -1)
DRIVER_MAJOR=$(echo "$DRIVER_VER" | cut -d'.' -f1)

if [ -z "$DRIVER_MAJOR" ]; then
    echo "ERROR: nvidia-smi not found. Switch to a GPU runtime (Runtime → Change runtime type → GPU)."
    exit 1
fi
echo "NVIDIA driver: ${DRIVER_VER} (major ${DRIVER_MAJOR})"

try_install () {
    apt-get -qq install -y "libnvidia-gl-${1}" >/dev/null 2>&1 && {
        echo "Installed libnvidia-gl-${1}"; return 0; }
    return 1
}

if ! try_install "${DRIVER_MAJOR}"; then
    echo "libnvidia-gl-${DRIVER_MAJOR} not in apt — scanning for any available major…"
    for cand in $(apt-cache search '^libnvidia-gl-[0-9]+$' \
                  | awk '{print $1}' | sed 's/^libnvidia-gl-//' | sort -rn); do
        try_install "$cand" && break
    done
fi

# Some Colab images install the userspace .so but skip the EGL ICD json;
# write it ourselves so libEGL knows the NVIDIA backend exists. Only write
# the ICD if libEGL_nvidia.so.0 is actually loadable — otherwise libEGL
# silently ignores it and we stay stuck on Mesa.
if ldconfig -p | grep -q libEGL_nvidia.so.0; then
    ICD=/usr/share/glvnd/egl_vendor.d/10_nvidia.json
    if [ ! -f "$ICD" ]; then
        mkdir -p "$(dirname $ICD)"
        printf '{"file_format_version":"1.0.0","ICD":{"library_path":"libEGL_nvidia.so.0"}}' > "$ICD"
        echo "Wrote $ICD"
    fi
else
    echo "ERROR: libEGL_nvidia.so.0 is still not on the loader path after install."
    echo "Available libnvidia-gl packages in apt:"
    apt-cache search '^libnvidia-gl-[0-9]+$' || true
    exit 1
fi

pip -q install moderngl==5.10.0 numpy

# --- Pull latest renderer source ---
# Hard-reset to origin/main so stale renderer.py copies from earlier sessions
# don't shadow the current EGL device-iteration logic.
if [ ! -d /content/music-viz ]; then
  git clone -q https://github.com/splice11/music-viz.git /content/music-viz
fi
cd /content/music-viz
git fetch -q origin main
git checkout -q -B main origin/main
git reset -q --hard origin/main

echo 'Setup complete.'</cell id="cell-2">
<cell id="cell-3"># Sanity-check: confirm the GPU EGL context is an NVIDIA device, not llvmpipe.
import sys
sys.path.insert(0, '/content/music-viz')
import moderngl

ctx = moderngl.create_context(standalone=True, backend='egl', require=330)
renderer = ctx.info.get('GL_RENDERER', '?')
version  = ctx.info.get('GL_VERSION',  '?')
ctx.release()

print('GL renderer:', renderer)
print('GL version :', version)

if 'llvmpipe' in renderer.lower() or 'softpipe' in renderer.lower():
    raise RuntimeError(
        "Still on software rendering (llvmpipe).\n"
        "1. Make sure you selected a GPU runtime (Runtime → Change runtime type → GPU).\n"
        "2. Re-run the Setup cell — the NVIDIA EGL ICD install may have needed a fresh session.\n"
        "3. If the problem persists, run: !ls /usr/share/glvnd/egl_vendor.d/ to check for 10_nvidia.json"
    )
else:
    print('\n✓ GPU context confirmed — rendering will use the hardware GPU.')</cell id="cell-3">
<cell id="cell-4"><cell_type>markdown</cell_type>## 2. Upload your song + analysis JSON

Drop in **both** files: the `.mp3` and the matching `viz_data_v2.json`.</cell id="cell-4">
<cell id="cell-5">import os, shutil
from google.colab import files
os.makedirs('/content/inputs', exist_ok=True)

uploaded = files.upload()
for name in uploaded:
    shutil.move(name, f'/content/inputs/{name}')
    print('saved →', f'/content/inputs/{name}')</cell id="cell-5">
<cell id="cell-6">import os, glob
mp3s = sorted(glob.glob('/content/inputs/*.mp3') + glob.glob('/content/inputs/*.wav') + glob.glob('/content/inputs/*.m4a'))
jsons = sorted(glob.glob('/content/inputs/*.json'))
assert mp3s,  'No audio file found in /content/inputs (mp3/wav/m4a).'
assert jsons, 'No JSON file found in /content/inputs.'
AUDIO_PATH = mp3s[0]
JSON_PATH  = jsons[0]
print('Audio:', AUDIO_PATH)
print('JSON :', JSON_PATH)</cell id="cell-6">
<cell id="cell-7"><cell_type>markdown</cell_type>## 3. Render — this is the long step

Defaults: 1920×1080 @ 60 fps, CRF 17 (visually lossless-ish). Drop to 1280×720 for a quick preview.</cell id="cell-7">
<cell id="cell-8">WIDTH       = 1920
HEIGHT      = 1080
TARGET_FPS  = 60
OUTPUT_PATH = '/content/cryogenic.mp4'

import importlib, sys
for m in list(sys.modules):
    if m.startswith('colab_render'):
        del sys.modules[m]
import colab_render

print('Building feature timeline…')
fd = colab_render.build(JSON_PATH, target_fps=TARGET_FPS)
print(f'  {fd.n_frames} frames @ {fd.fps:.0f} fps  ({fd.duration:.1f} s)')

print('Rendering…')
colab_render.render_to_video(
    fd,
    audio_path=AUDIO_PATH,
    out_path=OUTPUT_PATH,
    width=WIDTH, height=HEIGHT,
    crf=17, preset='medium',
    progress_every=120,
)</cell id="cell-8">
<cell id="cell-9"><cell_type>markdown</cell_type>## 4. Preview + download</cell id="cell-9">
<cell id="cell-10">from IPython.display import HTML
from base64 import b64encode
data = open(OUTPUT_PATH, 'rb').read()
src = 'data:video/mp4;base64,' + b64encode(data).decode()
HTML(f'<video width=720 controls src="{src}"></video>')</cell id="cell-10">
<cell id="cell-11">from google.colab import files
files.download(OUTPUT_PATH)</cell id="cell-11">